---
title: The W.E.F.T.
tags:
  - adventuring-party
campaigns: [deep-eyes]
date: 2025-05-05T00:00:00-04:00
---

The Weft is a collection of four to six adventurers that have traveled across [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]]. They're registered with [[Org/Althane/The Guild|The Guild]] and have completed some quests in the name of justice. Among them are [[People/Althane/Lev|Lev]], [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]], [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]], [[People/Althane/Dawnmonger|Dawnmonger]], and the [[Bestiary/Kaathe|Kaathe]] orbs [[People/Althane/Halidex Op-B|Hali]], [[People/Althane/Tennobrin Er-K|Tenno]] and [[People/Althane/SeRaan|SeRaan]].

They keep a base at [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/Lava Ruin/index|the lava ruin]], where the Heart they woke as [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/Lava Ruin/Damien|Damien]] forges items out of divine energy.

Immix named them "the Left" on a broadcast across [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]], showing a wanted-poster likeness of each of them beside a dossier of their deeds, their strength and the [[Phenomena/Althane/Godpiercer|godpiercer]] they hold. The same broadcast reaches [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]], where they are known as figures of Immix's talk show, [[Divinity/Immix|the Lighthouse]], and where their looks are worn by cosplayers. Divex wears the pearl [[People/Althane/Crystal Earring|Crystal Earring]], and the Weft carry a caged [[Bestiary/Mimics|tzitzimitl]]. They freed the Kaathe [[People/Althane/Halidex Op-B|Hali]] and [[People/Althane/Tennobrin Er-K|Tenno]] from the vats of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]], and both now travel with them.

General [[People/Althane/Karkov|Karkov]] named them the mongrels who killed his people, broke the First House beacon and stole the [[Phenomena/Althane/The Gun|gun]] the House kept, and their faces went out in flyers across [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]] to be hunted down and hanged in the streets. They killed him at RC3, and [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]] took his body.

All four carry the chrome of [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]] now: a skull implant, a subdermal piece, artificial lungs, and a port in the neck, cut in by [[People/Althane/The Broker|the Broker]]'s own hand. They can see the Rhett and hold credit there, and they pass for denizens of that planet.

They killed [[Divinity/Immix|Immix]] in the incomplete prison it kept, opening again the third observation of the [[Divinity/Althane/The Observers|Observers]] that Immix had taken. In the Observers' debt they are bound to hunt down and kill whoever next wrongs the pair, if they are able. From the Observers they bought a vision of the life of the being trapped at Althane's centre, [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|the Stranger]], and by it learned his true name.

They killed the Stranger at the centre of Althane, and keep their clones in coffins in an office whose owner none of them can name, with the golden needle in a drawer there. The warden of [[Geography/Althane/The Thirteenth Realm|the Thirteenth Realm]] once took them up to the station and gave them free run of it and its view over Althane.

They destroyed [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]] at the top of the City of Yellow, and the Thirteenth Realm's moon fell on the city in the same hour. The moon wiped the City of Yellow off [[Geography/Althane/Realms/Ilkyne|Ilkyne]], and the realm struck the planet and broke, leaving Ilkyne gone and the realm wreckage. The Weft walked out of the ruin into [[Phenomena/Althane/The Lighthouse|the Lighthouse]], rode it to a new crystal sphere it cracked open, and came back to Althane by its anchorways; the Lighthouse's central body has left the world, but its reach remains.

They spent a favor to speak to the whole of Althane at once, announced themselves as the Weft, and called the leaders of the world to a first council at [[Geography/Althane/Athrea/Thyropae/index|Thyropae]] in a hundred days.
